00:42:13,100 --> 00:42:16,060
And He says, though the earth be removed

692
00:42:16,060 --> 00:42:18,020
and though the mountains be carried

693
00:42:18,020 --> 00:42:19,460
into the midst of the sea,

694
00:42:19,460 --> 00:42:22,500
though the waters thereof roar and be troubled,

695
00:42:22,540 --> 00:42:26,460
though the mountains shake with the swelling thereof,

696
00:42:26,460 --> 00:42:30,380
Selah, meditate, think about this.

697
00:42:30,380 --> 00:42:33,460
Listen, He is our refuge, He is our strength,

698
00:42:33,460 --> 00:42:37,660
He is a very present help in the time of trouble.

699
00:42:37,660 --> 00:42:39,800
And He wants to meet your need this morning.

700
00:42:39,800 --> 00:42:41,360
And I don't even know, you say, pastor,

701
00:42:41,360 --> 00:42:42,200
you don't know my need.

702
00:42:42,200 --> 00:42:43,040
Can I tell you something?

703
00:42:43,040 --> 00:42:45,380
And I don't say this because I'm not compassionate.

704
00:42:45,380 --> 00:42:47,280
I don't really need to know your need.

705
00:42:48,740 --> 00:42:51,340
Now, it's okay if I do know what your need is

706
00:42:51,340 --> 00:42:54,060
and if I counsel you and give you direction

707
00:42:54,060 --> 00:42:55,180
and try to point you to the Lord.

708
00:42:55,180 --> 00:42:57,480
But listen, any of you that ever sat in my office

709
00:42:57,480 --> 00:42:59,180
for counsel, here's what I do.

710
00:42:59,180 --> 00:43:00,420
I'm not pointing you to me.

711
00:43:00,420 --> 00:43:01,340
I can't help you.

712
00:43:01,340 --> 00:43:02,700
I try to point you to God.

713
00:43:04,180 --> 00:43:05,200
Let's take the Bible.

714
00:43:05,200 --> 00:43:06,620
Let's try to help you understand

715
00:43:06,620 --> 00:43:08,520
here's what the word of God says.

716
00:43:08,520 --> 00:43:10,740
Some of you sat in my office for marriage counseling.

717
00:43:10,740 --> 00:43:13,180
I can't help your marriage, but God can.

718
00:43:13,180 --> 00:43:15,320
Some of you sat in my office because you got kid problems.

719
00:43:15,320 --> 00:43:18,300
I can't help your kids, but God can.

720
00:43:18,300 --> 00:43:19,140
Amen?

721
00:43:19,140 --> 00:43:20,220
And you go on and on and on.

722
00:43:20,540 --> 00:43:21,860
Financial, whatever it might be.

723
00:43:21,860 --> 00:43:25,380
I'm not a financial guy, but there are some Bible principles

724
00:43:25,380 --> 00:43:28,060
that God gives us that I could try to point you to

725
00:43:28,060 --> 00:43:28,880
and try to help you.

726
00:43:28,880 --> 00:43:29,720
Why?

727
00:43:29,720 --> 00:43:30,960
Because he can meet your needs.

728
00:43:33,660 --> 00:43:35,740
So here's what the psalmist says to wrap it all up

729
00:43:35,740 --> 00:43:36,700
in Psalm 121.

730
00:43:36,700 --> 00:43:38,740
You don't even need to turn there.

731
00:43:38,740 --> 00:43:43,180
But the Bible says, I will lift up mine eyes to the hills.

732
00:43:43,180 --> 00:43:44,500
Now think about it just for a moment.

733
00:43:44,500 --> 00:43:48,880
Where the disciples are, where Jesus was,

734
00:43:48,880 --> 00:43:52,040
he's in a mountain, he's praying.

735
00:43:52,040 --> 00:43:56,200
He saw them, he knew where they were,

736
00:43:56,200 --> 00:43:58,640
knew what they were facing, knew what they needed.

737
00:43:59,800 --> 00:44:03,160
Sometimes we're so much in the midst of the sea,

738
00:44:03,160 --> 00:44:05,920
and yes, we read this portion of scripture and we rejoice.

739
00:44:05,920 --> 00:44:07,960
Man, listen, this was recorded for us,

740
00:44:07,960 --> 00:44:09,840
but listen, it's recorded for us

741
00:44:09,840 --> 00:44:11,880
so that we could be helped in our storm.

742
00:44:13,480 --> 00:44:15,360
My storm's different than your storm,

743
00:44:15,360 --> 00:44:17,360
and all of our storms are different than the storm

744
00:44:17,360 --> 00:44:19,560
that they faced on the Sea of Galilee that day.

745
00:44:19,560 --> 00:44:20,400
Why?

746
00:44:20,400 --> 00:44:22,320
Because we're not in a boat going across the sea.

747
00:44:24,640 --> 00:44:25,880
We're facing storms.

748
00:44:27,940 --> 00:44:30,600
I will lift up mine eyes into the hills.

749
00:44:30,600 --> 00:44:32,240
From whence cometh my help?

750
00:44:33,120 --> 00:44:37,760
My help cometh from the Lord, which made heaven and earth.

751
00:44:37,760 --> 00:44:39,760
He's the creator God.

752
00:44:39,760 --> 00:44:40,720
Let there be light.

753
00:44:40,720 --> 00:44:41,840
There was light.

754
00:44:41,840 --> 00:44:44,000
He spoke it all into existence,

755
00:44:44,920 --> 00:44:47,280
and he's your helper, and he's my helper.

756
00:44:48,240 --> 00:44:51,840
For those disciples, toiling and rowing,

757
00:44:51,840 --> 00:44:53,760
the wind was contrary.

758
00:44:53,760 --> 00:44:56,680
They were just obeying what Jesus said,

759
00:44:56,680 --> 00:45:00,200
and they find themselves facing a great storm,

760
00:45:00,200 --> 00:45:01,840
and Jesus saw them.

761
00:45:03,080 --> 00:45:06,320
He saw them, and he knew what they were facing,

762
00:45:06,320 --> 00:45:08,240
that they were toiling and rowing.

763
00:45:08,240 --> 00:45:11,640
The winds were contrary, and he talked with them,

764
00:45:11,640 --> 00:45:13,720
and he spake unto them.

765
00:45:14,440 --> 00:45:18,320
He gave them a word, and then it says that he went up

766
00:45:18,320 --> 00:45:21,120
unto them, in verse number 51.

767
00:45:21,120 --> 00:45:23,200
Praise God for the fellowship.

768
00:45:23,200 --> 00:45:24,560
Abide in him.

769
00:45:25,400 --> 00:45:26,360
We can have that fellowship.

770
00:45:26,360 --> 00:45:28,760
He wants to meet your need this morning.

771
00:45:28,760 --> 00:45:30,040
I don't know what it is.

772
00:45:31,120 --> 00:45:34,740
I don't know what heartache you're carrying this morning,

773
00:45:34,740 --> 00:45:38,000
but I know that Jesus cares,

774
00:45:38,000 --> 00:45:40,160
and I know that he's able to give you

775
00:45:40,160 --> 00:45:42,200
exactly what you need.

776
00:45:42,200 --> 00:45:47,200
He said to Paul, my grace is sufficient for thee.

777
00:45:49,240 --> 00:45:51,000
That wasn't just a promise to Paul.

778
00:45:51,000 --> 00:45:52,800
That's a promise to each one of us.

779
00:45:54,100 --> 00:45:57,360
Remember that we're to come boldly

780
00:45:57,360 --> 00:46:00,760
unto the throne of grace, that we may obtain mercy,

781
00:46:00,760 --> 00:46:04,500
and find grace to help in time of need.

782
00:46:04,500 --> 00:46:07,880
I don't know what your need is in this time,

783
00:46:07,880 --> 00:46:10,880
but I know the one that can meet the need,

784
00:46:10,880 --> 00:46:13,240
and I wanted to point you to Jesus this morning,

785
00:46:13,240 --> 00:46:15,080
and I wanna encourage you this morning

786
00:46:15,080 --> 00:46:18,120
that he knows where you are, he knows what you're facing,

787
00:46:18,120 --> 00:46:19,160
and he knows what you need.

788
00:46:19,160 --> 00:46:20,000
Let's pray.

789
00:46:20,000 --> 00:46:21,120
Father, we love you.

790
00:46:21,120 --> 00:46:22,300
We thank you for loving us.

791
00:46:22,300 --> 00:46:24,420
We thank you for the word of God.

792
00:46:24,420 --> 00:46:26,160
Thank you for this portion of scripture,

793
00:46:26,160 --> 00:46:29,560
this passage, this record that you've given us

794
00:46:29,560 --> 00:46:32,960
of this event in the life of the disciples.

795
00:46:32,960 --> 00:46:34,560
As we think about this particular event,

796
00:46:34,560 --> 00:46:37,300
we're reminded of our own lives.

797
00:46:37,300 --> 00:46:39,000
God, in a crowd of any size,

798
00:46:39,000 --> 00:46:44,000
there's needs that are represented by people, real needs.

799
00:46:45,760 --> 00:46:48,120
Some greater than others, but all needs.

800
00:46:50,320 --> 00:46:52,440
Maybe somebody needs to be saved this morning.

801
00:46:52,440 --> 00:46:55,820
They've never trusted Jesus as their personal savior.

802
00:46:55,820 --> 00:46:57,800
I pray that in just a moment, they'd come to this altar,

803
00:46:57,800 --> 00:46:59,200
and we'd have an opportunity to take a Bible

804
00:46:59,200 --> 00:47:00,500
and show them how they could know for sure

805
00:47:00,500 --> 00:47:01,840
that heaven is their home.

806
00:47:03,620 --> 00:47:07,100
The list of needs is beyond my ability to exhaust,

807
00:47:07,940 --> 00:47:12,500
but I'm grateful to know that you as our lovingly,

808
00:47:13,620 --> 00:47:17,740
omniscient, compassionate God,

809
00:47:19,180 --> 00:47:22,540
that you know the needs of those that are here this morning.

810
00:47:22,540 --> 00:47:25,100
And God, I pray that in the moment

811
00:47:25,100 --> 00:47:28,340
that you'd move and work and help these folks,

812
00:47:28,340 --> 00:47:30,700
Lord, to do as the psalmist said in Psalm 121,

813
00:47:31,860 --> 00:47:33,140
to lift their eyes into the hills

814
00:47:33,140 --> 00:47:34,140
from whence cometh their help.

815
00:47:34,140 --> 00:47:37,580
Lord, help us to trust you and to hear from you

816
00:47:37,580 --> 00:47:41,160
and to apply the truth, that we'd receive the help,

817
00:47:41,160 --> 00:47:44,340
that we would not let you just pass on by,

818
00:47:44,340 --> 00:47:47,700
but that we'd willingly receive what you have for us.

819
00:47:49,260 --> 00:47:51,440
God, you'd help us as only you can.

820
00:47:52,320 --> 00:47:53,700
I pray that you'd be honored and glorified

821
00:47:53,700 --> 00:47:54,980
for it's in Christ's name we pray.

822
00:47:54,980 --> 00:47:56,900
Would you stand with me?

823
00:47:56,900 --> 00:47:58,260
Heads are bowed, eyes are closed,

824
00:47:58,260 --> 00:48:00,620
and just a moment, Kimberly's gonna play on the piano,

825
00:48:00,620 --> 00:48:02,380
and as she does, the altar will be open,

826
00:48:02,380 --> 00:48:04,220
and I wanna encourage you this morning,

827
00:48:04,220 --> 00:48:05,220
if you're not sure of heaven,

828
00:48:05,220 --> 00:48:07,140
today is the day of salvation.

829
00:48:07,140 --> 00:48:08,620
Mark is here if you're a man,

830
00:48:08,620 --> 00:48:09,980
and Brianna's here if you're a lady.

831
00:48:09,980 --> 00:48:11,460
Take a Bible, show you, you can know for sure

832
00:48:11,460 --> 00:48:12,700
that heaven is your home.

833
00:48:13,780 --> 00:48:15,180
Many of you, I know personally,

834
00:48:15,180 --> 00:48:16,820
I've heard your testimony as a salvation.

835
00:48:16,820 --> 00:48:18,680
I know you're saved.

836
00:48:18,680 --> 00:48:21,020
Maybe you came in here this morning with some needs,

837
00:48:21,020 --> 00:48:22,160
some heartache.

838
00:48:23,220 --> 00:48:24,300
Maybe you just need to come to this altar

839
00:48:24,300 --> 00:48:25,820
and get alone with the Lord,

840
00:48:25,820 --> 00:48:29,100
and get the help that only God can provide you with.

841
00:48:29,100 --> 00:48:31,500
As Kimberly plays, the altar is open.

